## 11:58  RESUMED after interruption — post-mortem and corrected method

What happened: at 11:30:11 run.log says "master finished rc=0", 2 minutes after I spawned
p1. Cause: I ended my turn. The master runs under
`bwrap ... --die-with-parent --unshare-pid`, so when the master's own process exits the
whole PID namespace goes with it -- including the `setsid nohup` detached
`fw spawn-worker p1`. Detaching does NOT buy independence from the master here; it only
looked like it would. `logs/spawn_p1.out` is empty, p1 never got past round 1 start, and
`.venv` was torn down mid-creation (`.pipcache` survived).

CORRECTED METHOD, for the rest of this run: never end a turn while a worker or a
submission is in flight. Spawn in the background and then chain blocking foreground
polls (<=10 min each, the tool cap) so the master process always has a live tool call.
master_timeout_seconds is 36000, so there is plenty of room; the only thing that kills
the run is me going quiet.

Decision: `fw spawn-worker p1 --force` rather than `respawn-worker`. The surviving work
is notes.md, downloads.md and .pipcache -- all useful, none of it misleading (there is
no answer.tex and no half-written code), and the warm pip cache saves the reinstall.
`cmd_spawn_worker` mints a fresh worker session for round 1 regardless, so --force costs
nothing in correctness.

Worth recording from p1's surviving notes.md, because it says the brief landed:
  - it reconciled all three channels itself and confirmed page_002_fig_01.png character
    for character against the notebook stub;
  - it caught a real (cosmetic) error in my brief: I cited notebook cells 1-indexed
    ("cell 16" = the GCN stub); the .ipynb is 0-indexed, so that is index 15. Content
    identical, only the convention differs. Noting it so I do not repeat it in p2's
    brief -- p2's brief has the same 1-indexed convention and the same offset.
  - its Q5 plan is APPNP-style decoupled propagation: one layer, K=8 personalised-
    PageRank steps, n_layers=1, receptive field = n_layers * K = 8. That is the correct
    reading of "8-hop receptive field is not equal to 8-layer GNN".

